<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  AS-063 (OPC 10000-3 section 7.17) - PASS case 2: a diamond is not a cycle.

  Plant notifies from both LineA and LineB, and both notify from the shared
  Machine. Machine is therefore reachable from Plant by two distinct paths,
  which section 7.17 explicitly permits: the rule forbids returning to the
  *origin*, not arriving at the same descendant twice.

  This is the case a naive "has this node been visited before" implementation
  reports as a loop. A shape that fails this fixture is rejecting the standard
  way an address space shares one Machine between two production lines.

  HasEventSource and HasNotifier are mixed here so both members of the shape's
  path alternation are exercised in the same graph.
-->
<UANodeSet xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
           xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
           xmlns="http://opcfoundation.org/UA/2011/03/UANodeSet.xsd">
